            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000:F004\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Under item (ii), subclauses (I) and (II) are disjunctive alternatives separated by 'or'. Subclause (II) permits inspection 'at any time with respect to records relating to a firearm involved in a criminal investigation that is traced to the licensee', whereas the 'not more than once during any 12-month period' limitation belongs exclusively to subclause (I). The proposed summary incorrectly applies the 12-month frequency restriction to firearm trace records under subclause (II), contradicting the statutory authority.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000:F004\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The draft claim C0002 leaves the action and action_quote empty. The source text in F000 explicitly provides that the Attorney General may 'inspect or examine' the inventory and records under the conditions specified in F002 and F004. Populating the action with exact quotation accurately captures the authorized conduct without altering or corrupting the claim's scope or conditions.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
